id: pm-vklr99
title: "Cross-process reproducibility gate: prove CLI and MCP deterministic runs are byte-identical and fail on ambient time leaks"
description: "Add a permanent release/CI acceptance gate that executes real CLI and MCP process workflows twice in isolated fresh workspaces with the same declared clock, tick, and seed, compares authoritative tracker and history bytes, and includes negative controls for invalid configuration and default-path variability."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-22T12:30:15.775Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-06T08:26:24.145Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-06T08:26:23.596Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-06T08:26:23.596Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: The gate runs real packaged CLI and MCP transports rather than calling the context primitive directly; two isolated same-configuration runs compare byte-identical authoritative item and history outputs; a negative control proves differing seeds or absent process configuration is observable; invalid and partial environment contracts are covered; the gate is invoked by an existing mandatory CI path and has focused unit coverage
goal: ci-detects-every-defect
objective: Turn process-level reproducibility from documentation into a mechanical release invariant
value: A future transport or timestamp call-site regression fails locally and in hosted CI with a replayable configuration
why_now: GH-1089 proves SDK-only tests can stay green while the shipped binary remains nondeterministic
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Scope SDK attribution to the selected tracker across CLI and MCP and pin a supported test session with an ambient attribution positive control.
expected_result: Conflicting ambient claims remain available to the test but cannot contaminate the explicitly selected tracker; CI must prove the ambient source exists.
actual_result: "188 linked process tests and an ordinary-CI environment run pass. Full suite: 8477 tests, 623 files, exact 100/100/100/100. Isolated unchanged import/transport timing, graph and record gates pass; contended timing failure retained."
