comments[21]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T12:30:15.775Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-22: all-status certified corpus and exact/fuzzy searches for deterministic CLI,MCP,golden-byte,conformance,and process gates found broader open simulators and format programmes but no bounded transport-level reproducibility gate. This task is the executable proof for pm-gh1089 and does not claim the much wider fault simulator pm-a8lnoh or full format suite pm-4jk8kx."
  "2026-08-22T12:46:28.753Z","harness:codex","Gate evidence: the first fresh-process comparison exposed a bundle-context split; after moving the boundary into cli/main, the next gate exposed seed reuse collisions across distinct CLI invocations. The final contract uses stable step-derived CLI seeds and one advancing process-lifetime MCP sequence. Focused verification passes 54 tests with byte-identical tasks/history and typed invalid-input recovery."
  "2026-08-22T12:54:19.957Z","harness:codex","Repository-wide suite evidence: 7,775/7,776 tests passed; the only failure was the intentional 120-file directory-cap contract after adding new SDK/unit files. Moved the adapter and unit gate into focused reproducibility subdirectories; the directory-cap contract and focused process suite now pass 27/27."
  "2026-08-22T13:01:45.614Z","harness:codex","Graph assurance remediation: the exact new prose gap was pm-vklr99 -> pm-a8lnoh, which the gate description explicitly contrasts as a larger simulator. Added a typed related edge; no baseline or exemption changed."
  "2026-08-22T13:02:00.859Z","harness:codex","Correction: the first dependency mutation was refused because the shorthand was invalid; the subsequent canonical id=pm-a8lnoh,kind=related mutation succeeded. The earlier comment's edge-added claim applies only after this successful receipt."
  "2026-08-22T13:31:02.413Z","harness:codex","Acceptance evidence: PM-linked command passed 177/177 across real fresh CLI/MCP process comparison, SDK resolver coverage, stdio fallback, and public CLI error rendering. Full corpus passed 559/559 files and 7,778/7,778 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. Independent mktemp smoke proved byte-identical tasks/history for two built-CLI workflows plus typed exit-2 recovery from both built CLI and MCP; bounded temporary data was deleted with find -P -xdev -depth -delete."
  "2026-08-22T13:50:10.582Z","harness:codex","Review remediation: the initial release occurred before expected_result and actual_result were appended. Reopened this canonical item, cleared and restored the complete validation fields through pm before renewed closure, and linked the generated CHANGELOG.md entry."
  "2026-08-22T13:58:29.207Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit remediation evidence: every real-process spawn is bounded at 30 seconds and assertion diagnostics include error, stdout, and stderr; strict clock negative controls cover timezone-less and parseable non-ISO values. PM-linked verification and the full 7,780-test corpus pass at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-09-06T06:17:34.628Z","harness:codex","New regression evidence in PR 1208: a full 8476-test run passed 8475 but failed byte comparison because subprocesses inherited a PM_PATH with no initialized settings and cwd was the real repository. Attribution fallback read the live repository runtime session, so concurrent review-item releases changed role/topic evidence between MCP runs. Reuse this canonical gate owner rather than create a duplicate. The clock/seed implementation is unchanged; the fixture must point all implicit reads at its own temporary tracker and workspace."
  "2026-09-06T06:20:54.452Z","harness:codex","Review fix verified: all linked process, SDK clock/seed, MCP handshake and CLI error tests pass. The MCP byte-comparison scenario changes a separate temporary tracker claim workset between equivalent runs and still produces identical authoritative records. This test isolation repair is included in PR 1208; no runtime reproducibility policy or comparison field was weakened."
  "2026-09-06T06:28:29.483Z","harness:codex","Consolidated review verification: 623/623 files and 8476/8476 tests pass at exact 100/100/100/100 (62643 statements, 47519 branches, 12984 functions, 60210 lines). The reproducibility fixture now isolates cwd and both tracker roots, disables external probes and rejects contamination from a changing unrelated workset. Full static quality and typecheck passed; post-closure defect evidence, docs/skills, ESLint and SDK surface checks pass. The second PR head will receive fresh hosted checks and explicit review triggers."
  "2026-09-06T07:05:42.919Z","harness:codex","Second-review TDD red: preserving the deliberately injected ambient PM_PATH reveals a real MCP attribution leak. Explicit tool arguments write to the intended temporary tracker, but the request detection environment still imports changing claims from the unrelated ambient tracker into history provenance. Fix the transport context supplied to the existing scoped identity primitive, retaining full byte comparisons and the conflicting environment input."
  "2026-09-06T07:25:57.868Z","harness:codex","Additional real-process negative control: a temporary CLI invocation with explicit --pm-path and conflicting ambient PM_PATH writes the correct destination but infers history topic/role from unrelated ambient claims. Two otherwise identical target histories differ as the ambient workset changes. Extend the existing process-isolation delivery to the CLI adapter using the public SDK harness-signal context; retain conflicting input in the regression instead of overwriting it."
  "2026-09-06T07:31:51.936Z","harness:codex","Green evidence: the linked process suite passes after extending both CLI and MCP dispatch through runWithHarnessDetectionSignals with the resolved tracker. The shared ambient-claims regression is parameterized across both transports and compares complete item/history bytes; the CLI negative control failed before the fix. Explicit tracker selection is preserved without mutating process.env. TypeScript and focused ESLint pass; the final complete coverage/static gates are being rerun for this consolidated source."
  "2026-09-06T07:41:27.695Z","harness:codex","Final consolidated verification: all 188 linked process tests pass; the full suite passes 8477 tests in 623 files with exact 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts. Independent temporary CLI checks report byte_identical=true despite changing ambient claims. Fresh npm and Bun installed close/evidence-update/history verification passes; npx and bunx packed smoke passes across 13 packages. TypeScript, focused ESLint and documentation links pass."
  "2026-09-06T07:42:15.654Z","harness:codex","Final static run passed ESLint, zero-duplicate/docstring assurance, contracts, context/token measurements and SDK import costs, then failed the transport timing gate: create best 424ms exceeded the unchanged 398ms ceiling while full coverage and packed-consumer acceptance were running concurrently. Those workloads have now completed. Rerun this timing gate in isolation plus the remaining graph/record checks; retain both receipts and do not alter the budget."
  "2026-09-06T07:43:18.616Z","harness:codex","The isolated CLI transport-floor rerun passes all six operations with the existing budgets. Remaining graph-composition and record-integrity checks pass, as does the post-closure defect-evidence gate (145 governed terminal defects, zero findings). This completes the static sequence after retaining the earlier contended timing failure; no budget or gate was weakened."
  "2026-09-06T08:01:05.628Z","harness:codex","Verification gap found during hosted wait: readAgentSemanticAttributionSync returns immediately without an agent instance, while the process fixture inherits the host session. The ordinary coverage job does not set CODEX_THREAD_ID (only separate host-isolation smoke steps do). Add a positive control proving a real ambient claim is present in an ambient mutation history, then pin a supported session in the fixture so both CLI/MCP negative controls remain effective on ordinary CI. This is a test-assurance correction under the same canonical owner."
  "2026-09-06T08:11:27.160Z","harness:codex","Strengthened process acceptance with an ambient-history positive control and a pinned supported session identity. Without any harness session, the new control fails before the change (host-control-red.log); after pinning identity it passes. This makes CLI/MCP isolation tests substantive on ordinary CI rather than relying on an inherited Codex session. Ambient author/topic environment overrides are cleared in the subprocess fixture."
  "2026-09-06T08:23:48.359Z","harness:codex","Fourth-round verification: all 188 linked process tests pass, including the positive control on ordinary CI; npm and Bun temporary installed consumers pass evidence-update/history-prefix acceptance, and packed npx/bunx smoke passes for 13 packages. Static checks pass through contract/tracker assurance but the SDK import-time gate fails under concurrent full coverage/package load (round4-static.log, ten entrypoints). This failed measurement is retained; unchanged import and CLI timing gates will be rerun in isolation after all CPU-heavy verification ends."
  "2026-09-06T08:25:58.308Z","harness:codex","Final isolated verification passes all 10 SDK import entrypoints and all 6 CLI transport operations with unchanged ceilings after CPU-heavy jobs ended. Graph composition and record integrity gates pass. The retained contended measurement remains documented. Full final coverage passes 8477 tests across 623 files with exact 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts; no threshold, inclusion rule, waiver or budget was relaxed."
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T13:31:02.944Z","harness:codex","A deterministic one-shot CLI process restarts its entropy sequence, so multi-step shell workflows need stable step-derived seeds. A serialized long-lived MCP transport should instead retain one validated process runner so its sequence advances across requests. Exercise both process lifetimes with authoritative byte comparisons; calling only the context primitive cannot prove the bundled transport boundary."
  "2026-09-06T06:20:53.342Z","harness:codex","A PM_PATH whose target has no settings can fall back to cwd discovery during attribution. Process tests must set cwd and both tracker environment roots per fixture, not only pass --pm-path to the command. Disable external probes and exercise a separate changing ambient tracker so process byte identity does not depend on the real workset."
  "2026-09-06T07:31:52.538Z","harness:codex","A subprocess fixture must preserve an intentionally conflicting PM_PATH when testing explicit tracker precedence. For ordinary runs, isolate cwd and both tracker roots. For precedence tests, compare authoritative history as unrelated ambient claims change; ID-only or item-only checks miss provenance leakage."
